{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And they went, etc. — so they did.</b> It was necessary to say <b>so they did</b>, and it would not have sufficed with what he had already said, ״וַיַּעֲשׂוּ״ etc. — to declare that they were vindicated in their actions regarding the commandments of HaShem, and that they did not understand anything that was not actually so in its meaning. And this would not have been heard from his saying ״וַיַּעֲשׂוּ etc. כַּאֲשֶׁר״ etc., for it is possible that the verse is stating what they themselves thought. Understand this:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:12.898157005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}